  'The main numerical controls of an augmented all-electron calculation are therefore not captured by one cutoff. Interstitial basis size, angular-momentum cutoff, sphere radii, radial meshes, core/semicore partitioning, linearization choices introduced in Chapter 17, Brillouin-zone sampling, and SCF thresholds can affect different observables independently.',
